HST Office: the Special Character dialog's search finds symbols by their Vietnamese names.

The search compared the text only with the English Unicode names, so "hộp kiểm", "dấu tích", "mũi tên" or "đồng"
found nothing. HST's svx/source/dialog/hstsymbolsearch.cxx (SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary) holds Vietnamese names
for about 35 symbols office users look for (check boxes, ticks, crosses, arrows, math signs, currency, №, •) and
matches any part of a name, ignoring case and diacritics, so "hop kiem" works too. Hook: SearchUpdateHdl lists a
character of the current font when its English name or one of its Vietnamese names matches.

License: the upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the hst* files are HST's.
